00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:45,000
They’ve got a story, but have lost the plot.

2
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Lost in La Mancha is a documentary film directed by Keith Fulton.

3
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Fulton and Pepe's 2000 documentary captures Terry Gilliam's attempt
to get The Man Who Killed Don Quixote off the ground.

4
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Back injuries, freakish storms, and more zoom in to sabotage the project.

5
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Narrator (voice), played by Jeff Bridges.

6
00:27:54,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Self, played by Johnny Depp.

7
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:39,000
Self, played by Vanessa Paradis.

8
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Self, played by Jean Rochefort.

9
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:57,000
Self - Writer & Director, played by Terry Gilliam.

10
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Self - Co-Writer, played by Tony Grisoni.

11
00:51:09,000 --> 00:51:15,000
Lost in La Mancha is a 2002 documentary film about Terry Gilliam's first attempt to make The Man Who Killed
Don Quixote, a film adaptation of the 1605/1615 novel Don Quixote by Miguel de Cervantes.

12
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:54,000
The documentary was shot in 2000 during pre-production and filming and it
was intended as a "making-of" documentary for the film.

13
01:00:27,000 --> 01:00:33,000
However, Gilliam's failure to complete his film resulted in the documentary filmmakers
retitling their work as Lost in la Mancha and releasing it independently.

14
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:12,000
Written and directed by Keith Fulton and Louis Pepe, Lost in La Mancha presents Gilliam's
effort to make Don Quixote as a parallel to Quixote's quest to become a hero.

15
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
It co-stars Johnny Depp, Jean Rochefort, and Vanessa Paradis, who
were cast as stars for The Man Who Killed Don Quixote.

16
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:30,000
It is narrated by Jeff Bridges.

17
01:19:03,000 --> 01:19:09,000
Gilliam ultimately succeeded in making The Man Who Killed
Don Quixote, which was released in 2018.

18
01:23:42,000 --> 01:23:48,000
Fulton and Pepe have made a follow-up documentary, titled He Dreams of Giants,
which covers Gilliam's entire scope of work on the Quixote project.

19
01:28:21,000 --> 01:28:27,000
The film explores themes of director, don quixote, cinema history.
